&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Strategic Deals Lead to originate, structure, and close complex infrastructure deals critical to Anthropic&#39;s compute, networking, and memory strategy. In this role, you will lead end-to-end deal execution — from initial term sheet through final agreement — working across internal and external stakeholders to secure the infrastructure capacity Anthropic needs to stay at the frontier of AI development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s AI models depend on large-scale, tightly coordinated infrastructure spanning accelerator clusters, high-speed interconnects, and memory subsystems. Ensuring we can access and deploy that infrastructure at scale requires sophisticated deal-making with some of the world&#39;s largest technology companies. You will work closely with engineering, finance, and legal teams to structure transactions, negotiate terms, and close agreements with hyperscalers, semiconductor manufacturers, networking vendors, and memory suppliers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is fundamentally about deal leadership — bringing together technical understanding, financial acumen, and negotiating skill to secure strategic infrastructure at the terms and timelines Anthropic requires. You will be an integral part of a team focused on ensuring Anthropic has the resources it needs to pursue its mission of developing safe, beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full deal lifecycle for complex infrastructure transactions — from opportunity identification and term sheet development through negotiation, execution, and close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and negotiate large-scale agreements with hyperscalers, AI infrastructure companies, telecom providers, semiconductor manufacturers, and memory suppliers across compute, networking, and memory domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and drive financial models, term analyses, and commercial frameworks to support deal structuring and inform executive decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical requirements from engineering into commercially viable deal structures and contractual terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain senior-level relationships with strategic counterparties to identify and advance deal opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Finance, and Engineering to align deal terms with Anthropic&#39;s technical, financial, and risk requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate vendor and partner proposals, identify risks and trade-offs, and drive toward optimal deal outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear reporting on deal status, risks, and strategic implications to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of leading and closing complex, high-value technology transactions or strategic agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience structuring and negotiating deals within the technology space (hyperscalers, AI infrastructure, semiconductors, networking, telecom, or data center infrastructure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling and analytical skills, including experience with deal economics, vendor financing structures, and investment analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in high-speed networking (InfiniBand, Ethernet, optical interconnects) or memory technologies (DRAM, HBM, or related); familiarity with compute or silicon development a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive complex negotiations with large, sophisticated counterparties to favorable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at or negotiating with hyperscalers, telecom providers, or AI infrastructure companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and executive presence, with the ability to influence senior stakeholders internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–10 years of experience in strategic deals, corporate development, investment banking, or business development roles at technology companies, hyperscalers, telecom companies, or AI infrastructure firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in corporate development, including experience with M&amp;amp;A or strategic investments in networking, storage, memory, or adjacent infrastructure domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI/ML infrastructure requirements, including training cluster design, network topology, and memory bandwidth and capacity constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with vendor financing, equipment leasing, or capital markets structures applied to infrastructure procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of supply chain dynamics for high-demand infrastructure components (CPUs, network ASICs, HBM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in technical due diligence or technology mergers and acquisitions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for Anthropic&#39;s mission and ensuring safe AI development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
