&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The web operations team is part of Anthropic&#39;s Creative Studio — the in-house team responsible for brand expression across Anthropic and Claude. We&#39;re responsible for how content gets built, published, and maintained across anthropic.com and claude.com, and we care deeply about quality, consistency, and getting things right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Web Producer to join us in a hybrid production and content role, working at the intersection of editorial precision, web craft, and operational coordination. You&#39;ll be a trusted partner to content teams across the company, helping them navigate the publishing process, execute content updates, and build out pages that meet our quality bar. You&#39;ll also play a key role in keeping our web operations running smoothly by triaging incoming requests, coordinating smaller projects, and supporting launches with careful QA. You won&#39;t just execute tasks — you&#39;ll help improve the publishing experience for everyone who depends on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and publish content across our CMS platforms, including assembling templated pages and maintaining content collections with accuracy and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the web intake queue by triaging requests from partners, setting clear expectations on scope and timing, and keeping work moving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform thorough QA across staging and production environments before content goes live, catching errors in copy, formatting, links, and rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support web launches and campaigns by coordinating content publishing across relevant surfaces and flagging risks before they become problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with marketers and content teams to help them work effectively within our web infrastructure — answering questions, providing guidance, and reducing friction in their publishing experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain documentation and training resources that help partners publish confidently and independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with design engineers and the broader web team to ensure content is implemented correctly and templates are used as intended&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the governance and training around publishing access and guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns in recurring requests or issues and surface opportunities to improve how we work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience publishing and building content in a CMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong attention to detail — you catch what others miss and hold a high quality bar for anything that goes live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience coordinating requests or projects across multiple stakeholders with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a clear communicator who can set expectations, provide updates, and explain technical concepts to non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can document processes and create training materials that help others work more independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with headless CMS platforms (contentful, sanity etc…) and component-based design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in web production, content operations, or digital publishing at a technology company or agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building pages using structured templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with basic HTML/CSS sufficient to identify and communicate rendering issues to engineering and design partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using project management or ticketing tools (such as Asana, Linear, or Jira) to manage and prioritize a request queue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of SEO best practices as they apply to content structure, metadata, and page assembly&lt;/li&gt;
